 ## Overview
-STEVE is a 4D protomesh-based algorithm that generates iso-hypersurfaces from 4D volumetric data by transforming boundary cube octants into tetrahedrons [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like [Generalized Marching Cubes](8320-generalized-marching-cubes.md) by using a single 4D building block and a directed vector path system rather than a massive lookup table of configurations, thereby avoiding the exponential storage requirements of template-based approaches [S1, unofficial].
+STEVE is a 4D protomesh-based iso-hypersurface construction algorithm that generates iso-hypersurfaces from 4D volumetric data by transforming boundary cube octants into tetrahedrons [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from its siblings by using a single 4D building block to continuously transform identified boundary octants into final tetrahedrons, explicitly handling topological ambiguities to prevent accidental rifts in the resulting hypersurfaces [S1, unofficial]. Unlike template-based methods like MCA, STEVE relies on directed vector paths rather than a massive lookup table of configurations [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input:** A 4D scalar field (toxels) defined on a grid.
-*   **Output:** A set of tetrahedrons representing the iso-hypersurface.
